<body>
<div data-lys>
<article aria-label=\"What we know and what is needed\" data-notes=\"North's survey suggests installer scheduling is the leading reported barrier within its 40 respondents (28 selections), but selections overlap. South's 9 of 15 reviewed cases mentioning installer wait is a different unit and incomplete review, so the sources cannot be combined or ranked overall. Turnaround is a recent median of 8 days among 11 cases with recorded times; four lacked times. The spring estimate is unmethoded and not comparable. Need harmonized reporting and baseline data.\">
<section class=\"slide\">
<header>
<p class=\"kicker\">Program leads · evidence check</p>
<h1>Installer scheduling leads North’s survey; overall ranking and improvement remain unknown</h1>
<p class=\"sub\">The two partner summaries use different units and methods, and neither provides a comparable before-and-after turnaround measure.</p>
</header>
<div class=\"grid\">
<section class=\"panel north\" aria-labelledby=\"north-title\">
<h2 id=\"north-title\">Partner North · homeowner survey</h2>
<div class=\"stat\"><strong>28 / 40</strong><span>selected installer scheduling</span></div>
<div class=\"rows\" aria-label=\"North survey barrier selections\">
<div class=\"row primary\"><span>Installer scheduling</span><b>28</b></div>
<div class=\"row\"><span>Upfront cost</span><b>17</b></div>
<div class=\"row\"><span>Unclear eligibility</span><b>9</b></div>
</div>
<p class=\"note\">Multiple selections allowed; counts overlap and total more than 40. This is the most selected listed barrier within North’s survey only.</p>
</section>
<section class=\"panel south\" aria-labelledby=\"south-title\">
<h2 id=\"south-title\">Partner South · open case review</h2>
<div class=\"stat\"><strong>9 / 15</strong><span>cases mentioned waiting for an installer</span></div>
<div class=\"metric\"><strong>8 days</strong><span>median turnaround · 11 cases with a recorded time</span></div>
<p class=\"note\">Four of 15 cases had no time recorded. “Around two weeks last spring” has no identified cases, sample size, or method, so it is not a comparable baseline. Homeowners served in the period were not reported.</p>
</section>
</div>
<section class=\"callout\" aria-label=\"Answer and information needed\">
<div><h2>What can be answered</h2><p>North’s most selected listed barrier was installer scheduling. Which barrier is most common overall, and whether turnaround improved, cannot be established from these summaries.</p></div>
<div class=\"need\"><h2>To answer both parts</h2><ul><li>Use a shared period definition and denominator across partners; define how overlapping barrier selections are counted.</li><li>Report complete turnaround times with sample size and missingness, plus a baseline measured with the same method.</li></ul></div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
